      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if this cast can be avoided by ensuring that the `#[cxx::bridge]`-defined `enum` has a matching representation - see https://cxx.rs/shared.html#:~:text\u003dBy%20default%20CXX%20represents%20your%20enum%20using%20the%20smallest%20integer%20type%20capable%20of%20fitting%20all%20the%20discriminants%20(whether%20explicit%20or%20implicit).%20If%20you%20need%20a%20different%20representation%20for%20reasons%2C%20provide%20a%20repr%20attribute:\n\n```\n#[cxx::bridge]\nmod ffi {\n    #[repr(u32)]  // \u003c\u003d\u003d Would this let us avoid the `static_cast`?\n    enum Enum {\n        Zero,\n        One,\n        Five \u003d 5,\n        Six,\n    }\n}\n```",
